{
 "encounter_id": "00908",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Morning. I want to stop smoking, and I need help, because I can't do it on my own."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's a great decision, and I'm glad you came. How much do you smoke at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About twenty a day. Sometimes more when I'm stressed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long have you been smoking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Since I was seventeen. So, twenty-two years."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you tried to quit before? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Twice. Once with patches, and once cold turkey. I lasted a week each time. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What made you go back? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Stress at work, and my partner smokes too. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you cough in the mornings, or get breathless on the stairs?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit breathless on the stairs, yes. And a smoker's cough in the morning."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain, or coughing up blood?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Are you on any medication at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Just an inhaler, the blue one, when I'm wheezy."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your pulse, pressure and oxygen level. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sure.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 80, blood pressure 130 over 84, oxygen saturation 97 percent, temperature 36.6."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that all right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Reasonable. I'd like to listen to your chest. Take a few deep breaths for me. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "In and out?",
   "pause": 16.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There is a mild wheeze at the bottom of both lungs, and the breath sounds are otherwise normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's the smoking, isn't it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It is likely to be contributing. Stopping will help it settle."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What are my options, doctor? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There are nicotine patches and gum together, or a tablet called varenicline. I'd suggest we start with varenicline and combine it with support."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Does it have side effects? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Some people get nausea or strange dreams. Take it after food with a full glass of water. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I can manage that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll prescribe varenicline, 0.5 mg once a day for three days, then it goes up."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And when do I stop smoking? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pick a quit date in the second week, and take the tablets for the first week before that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. I'm going to say the fifteenth. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's good. I'd also like to see you again in two weeks, to see how it is going."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks, then. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
